      "description": "**`frontend/src/server/routes/providers.ts`** — 20 functions.\n\n- **`USE *`** · line 16 — Most routes require authentication (runs before every `/api/providers` route)\n- **`isOrgAdmin`** · line 64 — Check if user is an admin/owner of the current organization Returns true if personal context (no org) or if user is admin/owner\n- **`GET /`** · line 101 — List user's connected providers When in organization context, returns org-scoped providers with user's enabled preference When in personal context, returns personal providers (organizationId is null) (API route `GET /api/providers`)\n- **`GET /:id`** · line 164 — Get single provider details Returns provider info with account details (API route `GET /api/providers/:id`)\n- **`POST /connect/:type`** · line 235 — ✎ Starts Google OAuth for AdMob or Ad Manager; admins only in a team. The `state` isn't signed or stored (tour 14). (API route `POST /api/providers/connect/:type`)\n- **`GET /callback/:type`** · line 289 — ✎ Google's redirect: decodes the state, swaps the code for tokens, encrypts and saves them (tour 14). (API route `GET /api/providers/callback/:type`)\n- **`GET /:id/apps`** · line 437 — List apps for an AdMob provider SECURITY: Validates provider belongs to user's current org context (API route `GET /api/providers/:id/apps`)\n- **`DELETE /:id`** · line 546 — Disconnect provider Requires org admin role when in organization context SECURITY: Validates provider belongs to user's current org context (API route `DELETE /api/providers/:id`)\n- **`PATCH /:id/toggle`** · line 582 — Enable/disable provider for user's queries This is a per-user preference, any org member can toggle for themselves (API route `PATCH /api/providers/:id/toggle`)\n- **`GET /:type/token`** · line 641 — Get valid access token (auto-refreshes if needed) Used by internal services (LangGraph, MCP) to get tokens without manual refresh SECURITY: Validates provider belongs to user's current org context (API route `GET /api/pr